markdown <<MARKDOWN
<h1>Understanding How <code style="font-size:1em;">if</code> and <code style="font-size:1em;">while</code> Work Together</h1>
<p>Throughout this lesson, we've explored the key differences between if statements and while loops.</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">• <code style="font-size:14px;">if</code> statements check a condition once and execute the code if it's true.</p>
<p style="margin: 0;">• <code style="font-size:14px;">while</code> loops continue running as long as the condition remains true, making them useful for repeating actions.</p>
<p>These two structures often work together in a program. For example, an <code style="font-size:14px;">if</code> statement can check a condition inside a <code style="font-size:14px;">while</code> loop to decide when to stop or when to adjust behavior.</p>

<p>Let's trace through how this actually plays out, pass by pass.</p>

---

